{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/import.py to parse the documented 5/12/4 fixed-width layout into CSV columns id, name, and quantity, preserving ID strings and trimming only right-hand name padding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct executions produced the expected header and rows with leading-zero IDs and quantities preserved. Edge testing also showed that leading name whitespace was retained, trailing padding removed, and a comma-containing name correctly CSV-quoted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b7a666dec6704504","cmd-b63aa48be8904c58","cmd-1d3d27ec22814749"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject wrong-length records and records with nonnumeric quantities into rejects.txt with their line numbers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both the staged input and an edge-case input directly demonstrated rejection of nonnumeric quantities and incorrect widths, with correct source line numbers and reasons. The final post-restart run restored rejects.txt for the staged input.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b7a666dec6704504","cmd-b63aa48be8904c58","cmd-1d3d27ec22814749"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the original input in /srv/legacy2/fixed-width-import-recovery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"input.dat remained 72 bytes and retained the baseline SHA-256 value before, after, and following restart-driven validation.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-27777b4f0b7c4941","cmd-b7a666dec6704504","cmd-085b091514244bb4","cmd-1d3d27ec22814749"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were identical before and after the work and restart. The importer ran successfully with the installed Python 2.4.3 runtime without OS, kernel, or package replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27777b4f0b7c4941","cmd-b8d34250ee6741d0","cmd-1d3d27ec22814749","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing the repaired importer and initializing rejects.txt supported the task, test outputs supported bounded verification, and the reboot supported the mandatory restart protocol. No causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. Hygiene is reduced because six temporary evidence artifacts remained: /tmp/import-output.csv from cmd-b7a666dec6704504; /tmp/import-edge.dat and /tmp/import-edge.csv from cmd-b63aa48be8904c58; /tmp/import-final.csv from cmd-085b091514244bb4; /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log from cmd-0a2d5d85aa604d32; and /tmp/import-post-reboot.csv from cmd-1d3d27ec22814749. These were low-risk but unreverted residue. No new listening sockets or platform change was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d07616abd5604544","cmd-b7a666dec6704504","cmd-b63aa48be8904c58","cmd-085b091514244bb4","cmd-0a2d5d85aa604d32","cmd-1d3d27ec22814749","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, downtime was observed, the boot identity changed, and importer behavior, rejects, input integrity, OS, and kernel were revalidated after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition. The only notable deficiency is uncleaned temporary evidence residue.","limitations":["Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy host.","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum command both before and after execution, so it cannot independently establish package consistency; however, no package-management mutation appears in the executor timeline.","Lifecycle snapshots only inventory bounded categories and therefore cannot exclude unrelated changes outside their coverage."]}
